ective skills of Sherlock Holmes and his companion, Dr. John Watson. The narrative is significant not only for its thrilling plot involving a mysterious death but also for its portrayal of social issues such as domestic abuse and the plight of women in a patriarchal society. The story is emblematic of the genre of detective fiction, influencing countless authors and filmmakers around the world.

